<title>UK: UK's Brown pledges tough inflation target.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown pledges tough inflation target.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gordon Brown, finance spokesman for Britain's opposition Labour party, said he would set an inflation target as tough as the 2.5 percent target of the Conservative government.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be a tough inflation target,&quot; he told BBC radio, adding he would announce the target in a speech at 1800 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be as tough a target as the Conservatives'. But of course I think we can be tougher in bearing down on inflation by getting the institutional foundations of an anti-inflation policy right.&quot;  </p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
